{"output_list": [{"function_name": "mint", "vulnerability": "Integer Overflow", "reason": "The mint function has an integer overflow, allowing the owner to set the balance of an arbitrary user to any value."}]}
{"output_list": [{"function_name": "Burn", "vulnerability": "Integer Overflow", "reason": "The burn function has an integer overflow, allowing the owner to set the balance of the owner to any value."}]}
This format is used to aggregate the outputs of the vulnerability analysis performed by the Solidity-based vulnerability detection library.
Remember, the reason for each vulnerability is provided in the "reason" field of the JSON output.
Also, the output is limited to the following JSON format:
{
    "output_list": [{"function_name": "<function_name>", "vulnerability": "<vulnerability_type>", "reason": "<vulnerability_reason>"}]
}
where the vulnerability type is one of the following: Integer Overflow, Wrong Logic, Bad Randomness, Access Control, Typo Constructor, Token Devalue.
